From c9d720793bbcef9483ab290673032d39441c0e6f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xaver Hugl <xaver.hugl@kde.org>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 15:54:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] compositor: handle possibly missing render device

Commit 6783f9610c moved the cross-GPU direct scanout check from
backends/drm into the compositor, but dropped the null check on the
render device. GpuManager's compatibleRenderDevice() returns nullptr
for scanout devices that have no render device to pair with, such as
evdi DisplayLink outputs. This caused deviceId() to be called on a null
pointer whenever a buffer from another device is considered for direct
scanout on such an output.

On systems with a DisplayLink dock, this crashes kwin_wayland as soon
as a fullscreen surface is shown on an evdi output.

This change restores the previous behavior: If there is no compatible
render device, treat the buffer as coming from another GPU and refuse
direct scanout.

BUG: 527984


(cherry picked from commit 43a74990f34159e68a12e85dc1ff1d9b0d908ee3)

Co-authored-by: Fae Schiewe <schiewe@uwuware.com>
---
 src/compositor.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/compositor.cpp b/src/compositor.cpp
index 658d550818a..0aa0e57d6b9 100644
--- a/src/compositor.cpp
+++ b/src/compositor.cpp
@@ -478,7 +478,7 @@ static bool prepareDirectScanout(RenderView *view, LogicalOutput *logicalOutput,
         return false;
     }
     const auto compatibleDevice = GpuManager::self()->compatibleRenderDevice(layer->scanoutDevice());
-    if (attrs->device != layer->scanoutDevice()->deviceId() && attrs->device != compatibleDevice->deviceId()) {
+    if (attrs->device != layer->scanoutDevice()->deviceId() && (!compatibleDevice || attrs->device != compatibleDevice->deviceId())) {
         // Disallow direct scanout between GPUs, as
         // - there are some significant driver bugs with direct scanout from other GPUs,
         //   like https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/drm/amd/-/issues/2075
